                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                        "entry_id": "1fe2f9a9-f64f-36b4-8091-29b54c2fb858",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Enfant de genre indéterminé ou non-binaire de la sœur, du frère ou de l’adelphe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c340b6c5-de8a-4188-a8f8-0d34a91464b4",
                                "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                                "text": "j'explique à mes niblings la PMA et mon neveu croyait qu'on pouvait choisir toutes les caractéristiques du bébé, j'ai dû expliquer le principe d'eugénisme dans la foulée être tatie lesbienne c'est un job à temps plein"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f29e9d4-c864-454a-b061-a248018fb0fb",
                                "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                                "text": "Mon nibling et moi on a fait des tests random et les résultats sont a moitié drole a moitié réel"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59baa79f-ede7-415f-9877-d8fb613e2431",
                                "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                                "text": "Je dois accompagner mes niblings au ciné aujourd'hui priez pour pas que des p-word m'attaquent 🫡"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e64024b-d3fe-4688-bae5-4e1ef1bd0979",
                                "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                                "text": "Déjà je vois trop de trucs qui m'insupportent concernant maon nibling je deviendrais encore plus dingue que je ne le suis déjà"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd781c86-9fe7-481d-b8cd-5734bb2cf336",
                                "sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                                "text": "Jennifer Lopez a publié un court-métrage poignant qui met en scène Brendon, son \"nibling\" trans, et raconte son coming-out auprès de sa famille. Puissant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c876531-cc74-4d6d-a924-d374d3e89571",
                        "source_entry_id": "1fe2f9a9-f64f-36b4-8091-29b54c2fb858",
                        "source_sense_id": "1efcac38-572b-3247-b1fb-f1f8267c8dd1",
                        "target_lang_word": "nibling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nibling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                        "entry_id": "f9d948fa-7aab-3f16-8473-4fe019848443",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used especially as a gender-neutral term: the child of one's sibling or sibling-in-law; one's nephew or niece."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e8cf852-b53c-41f2-845e-161cc6dc7649",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "Aunts and uncles are concerned with the education of their niblings and may play a minor role in the ultimate arrangement of a marriage for the nibling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca29f510-8563-4dbd-9dad-8022c811dff0",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "Very recently I heard an informant respond with cousin to my question about the “child of nibling” position."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53d8c106-dc41-4409-871f-2dae8bef0c94",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "In the following line we find Q¹P²; that is, child of a parent of a parent; this is the relation that nuncles (aunts or uncles) bear to niblings (nieces or nephews)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bea7271c-c27b-4be5-a8b1-05607f7c0e34",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "She [Viola Edmundson Garfield] was close to her family, particularly her younger “siblings and niblings.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a940961-436e-40b4-b8be-49fd55cdaa52",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "Kin selection was strongest for choices between sibling and friend, decreasing across sibling vs. nibling, nibling vs. friend, and nibling vs. cousin, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24690b04-c709-4c18-9dc4-32e536853bf7",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "Most distinctive of the system, therefore, were the two terms for parental siblings and for niblings, which occurred only among the Salish and neighboring Southern Nootkans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48f13df1-3dcf-4f11-b07c-5c9f81645854",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "But, it is my niblings who taught me how to love."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e3ed534-0676-4363-9ea6-6107011915ee",
                                                "sense_id": "7e12ed91-e92c-3f4c-8c18-5888bd730cd8",
                                                "text": "Cousins are informally referred to by the same terms used for siblings, but officially one has an aunt/uncle-nibling relationship with one's cousins."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
